[{:adr/pattern-9511 "sealed RepairOps-LLM + independent Repair Governor + append-only audit ledger, modeled closely on the repair-shop-cluster's own architecture and the 85 other prior actors; EIGHTY-SIXTH actor in this fleet (85 implemented before this build)", :adr/test-example-swap-9511 "kotoba-lang/industry's own test/kotoba/industry_test.clj hardcoded \"9511\" as its still-blueprint example in 3 assertions (a leftover from the prior turn's own 9523-promotion swap) -- since 9511 was the id being promoted in this same commit, all 3 references were swapped to \"9101\" (Community Library and Archive, a gftdcojp-origin entry verified to have the IDENTICAL generic required-technologies stack [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger] and its own :repo field, so :has-repo?/ui-ready?/export-ready? assertions remain valid)", :adr/honest-reuse-checks-9511 "parts-cost-matches-claim? and safety-test-not-passed are HONEST, LITERAL reuses of the repair-shop-cluster's own checks for the SAME real-world concerns, reapplied to ICT-equipment-repair tickets (storage drives, power supplies, motherboards, displays) rather than consumer-electronics, communication-equipment, household-appliance, furniture, watch/jewelry/bicycle or footwear/leather-goods repair tickets -- NOT claimed as new", :adr/related ["2607071849-cloud-itonami-repairshop-9521-coverage" "2607086600-cloud-itonami-commrepair-9512-coverage" "2607086700-cloud-itonami-applianceshop-9522-coverage" "2607087200-cloud-itonami-furniture-9524-coverage" "2607087300-cloud-itonami-specialtyrepair-9529-coverage" "2607087400-cloud-itonami-leathergoods-9523-coverage" "2607032000-cloud-itonami-insurance-real-estate-coverage" "cloud-itonami-isic-6511 through 9529 and 9523 ADR-0001s (85 prior actors)" "langgraph ADR-0001"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "2607091400", :adr/fleet-maturity-before "{:implemented 85, :blueprint 13, :spec 545, :total 643}", :adr/next-vertical-selection-unconstrained true, :adr/distinctive-check-9511 "media-sanitization-unconfirmed-violations is a GENUINELY NEW concept (grep-verified absent fleet-wide -- zero hits for any governor check function named 'media-sanitiz'/'secure-disposal'/'800-88'/'data-destruction'), the 70th distinct application of the unconditional-evaluation discipline overall (casualty.governor/sanctions-violations's original fix; most recently leathergoods.governor/brand-authenticity-unconfirmed-violations at 69th), the SEVENTH conditional variant (after socialresearch/7220's, bizassoc/9411's, training/8549's, furniture/9524's, specialtyrepair/9529's and leathergoods/9523's own, at 63rd, 64th, 66th, 67th, 68th and 69th) -- CONDITIONAL on a ticket's own involves-storage-replacement? ground truth (a screen or battery repair has no media-sanitization concern at all). EXPLICITLY read commrepair/9512's own full governor.cljc before finalizing this check: commrepair/9512 already has a customer-data-consent-unconfirmed-violations check (grounded in the FTC's 'Nixing the Fix' report, GDPR, DSGVO, 個人情報保護法), evaluated UNCONDITIONALLY, addressing consent to ACCESS data DURING repair. This new check addresses a DIFFERENT real-world moment -- secure DESTRUCTION of a REMOVED storage component AFTER the repair decision to replace it -- a distinct duty, not a rehash. Grounded in real media-sanitization/data-destruction law: NIST SP 800-88 Rev.1 (enforced via the US FTC's FACTA Disposal Rule, 16 C.F.R. Part 682), UK GDPR Article 5(1)(f)/Article 32 (enforced by the ICO), Germany's DSGVO Art. 32 / BDSG (enforced by the BfDI), and Japan's own 個人情報保護法 (APPI) 安全管理措置 requirements (enforced by 個人情報保護委員会) -- ALL FOUR seeded jurisdictions actually have a real regime here, reported honestly (matching leathergoods/9523's own full-coverage brand-authenticity sub-citation, rather than forcing an artificial single-jurisdiction gap)", :adr/fleet-maturity-after "{:implemented 86, :blueprint 12, :spec 545, :total 643}", :adr/fresh-governor-no-collision-9511 "unlike the :