o this scope via an AskUserQuestion at the close of the prior turn (\"Extend into gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-* (Recommended)\")", :adr/deepened-to-implemented "cloud-itonami-isic-9511", :adr/no-bespoke-capability-lib-9511 "this blueprint's own :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies names no domain-specific capability beyond the generic robotics/identity/forms/dmn/bpmn/audit-ledger stack -- there was no capability-lib decision to make at all", :adr/test-status-9511 "40 tests / 192 assertions, lint clean, demo verified end-to-end (one clean dual-actuation lifecycle plus five HARD-hold cases); kotoba-lang/industry's own full test suite re-run with the local-root technology override before committing -- 7 tests / 133 assertions, all green", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isic-9511 (community ICT equipment repair) deepened to :implemented -- first build in the gftdcojp-origin-registry scope extension", :adr/blueprint-already-correct-9511 "this repo's blueprint.edn already had the correct :required-technologies matching the kotoba-lang/industry registry's own entry for \"9511\" exactly (its own :optional-technologies [:optimization] is registry-only, not required for readiness) -- only the :maturity field itself needed adding"}]